Jamia looks like something landed there  extremely quickly and skidded to a halt  maybe something had crashed here the  crash theory gains traction when  investigators discover the image is  taken close to the site of one of the  world's most catastrophic aviation  accidents so when you think about  something crashing in that part of the  world you think about the worst air  disaster in New Zealand history at 7:21  a.m. on November 28th 1979 Air New  Zealand flight 901 takes off from  Auckland Airport on a sightseeing tour  of Antarctica  the crew report clear weather and good  visibility but as the plane nears Mount  Erebus a strange and terrifying optical  illusion known as a whiteout deceives  the two pilots it's not a storm it's  simply a situation where there's white  everywhere white glacier beneath white  clouds above and there's no way to tell  what's up what's down and what's in  front of you at 12:49 p.m. the plane  plows into the ice killing all 257  passengers and crew  BAM they just smashed into the side of  Mount Erebus traveling hundreds of miles  per hour for the pilots it must have  been horrifying those last few seconds  realizing that out of nowhere a  mountainside was looming in the cockpit  window analyst Mark Dantonio studies the  image to see if it could be a remnant of  the plane's long debris trail he  discovers something isn't right when you  first look at this it looks as if  somebody was scraping along in the ice  and making this gigantic furrow but if  we look at this object over here this  little spire of rock you see the shadow  which way it's going well there we see  the shadow as well this is an elevated  feature this is an elevated feature too  the shadow indicates it is not a  depression in the ice but something  rising above it  nasa scientist dr. kelly brunt travels  to the remote feature she finds a seven  mile long wall of jagged ice protruding  from the frozen seas of McMurdo Sound  just like an ice cube in a glass about  10% of the ice is above the surface and  the other 90% is below the surface the  massive ice wall is a rare type of  glacier called an ice tub created by  millions of tons of ice flowing from the  base of Mount Erebus into the frozen  seas
 

